# graphify-specific exclusions (gitignore syntax) — content that's tracked in
# git (so .gitignore doesn't touch it) but isn't application code/architecture
# docs, and pollutes query/explain results with the tool's own self-referential
# output when ingested as if it were part of the codebase.

# Per the docs/ convention in CLAUDE.md, only docs/architecture/ describes
# what is actually built. docs/intent/ and docs/in_progress/ are unbuilt
# aspiration (future state / active plans, not current fact), and
# docs/experiments/, docs/plans/, docs/agent/ are process/tool write-ups, not
# architecture. Ingesting any of these as if they were current-state facts
# pollutes query/explain results with plans, prose, and self-referential
# graphify commentary that hasn't been (or won't be) built. A query should
# only ever reflect the current state of the system.
#
# `docs/*` (no trailing slash) matches only docs' direct children as a glob,
# so it never excludes the `docs/` directory itself - traversal continues and
# the negation below can still re-include one child's subtree.
docs/*
!docs/architecture/

# The `impeccable` design-critique skill's own generated report output
# (timestamped critique markdown files) — tool-generated artifacts, not
# authored documentation, analogous to graphify's own graphify-out/.
.impeccable/
